      "rev_n_19_04b3fa_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_19_04b3fa_1",
        "node_id": "n_19_04b3fa",
        "thought_text": "The previous approach using the number of set bits in the binary representation of the absolute difference between a and b is incorrect. The error occurs because it doesn't account for the fact that we can perform operations on both numbers simultaneously. Instead, we should consider the sum of the binary representations of a and b, as each set bit in either number contributes to the total number of operations needed.",
